WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.731
Take a single mesh from a practice
pack and add it to your Unreal project.

2
00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:09.840
On the Forage beta page, enter your email
and choose “Email my beta link.”

3
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:15.438
Open the link in your inbox, then download
the Windows ZIP for your Unreal version.

4
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:20.611
Close Unreal. In Windows, open the folder
that contains your project file.

5
00:00:20.961 --> 00:00:26.251
Open Plugins, or create that folder.
Extract the entire ForageBeta folder here.

6
00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:30.335
Check that ForageBeta.uplugin
is directly inside it.

7
00:00:30.985 --> 00:00:35.209
Open the project, choose Edit → Plugins,
and search for Forage Beta.

8
00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:38.695
Enable the plugin and restart
Unreal when prompted.

9
00:00:39.345 --> 00:00:42.395
Open Window → Forage → Guided Tutorial.

10
00:00:43.045 --> 00:00:47.269
The first dialog offers to stage
the practice mesh and its dependencies.

11
00:00:47.619 --> 00:00:52.441
Choose Yes. The staging folder is
under Saved/ForageBeta in your project.

12
00:00:53.091 --> 00:00:58.040
Review the three filenames. Choose Yes again
to add them to the project's Content folder.

13
00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:03.703
Unreal selects the token mesh. Its material
and texture are in the same folder.

14
00:01:04.353 --> 00:01:07.937
Drag the mesh into the viewport.
You've added the token to your level.

15
00:01:08.587 --> 00:01:13.558
To explore your own project's assets,
open Window → Forage → Open Dashboard.

16
00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:18.837
Choose Check for Updates in the Forage menu
to see whether a newer version is available.

17
00:01:19.187 --> 00:01:23.603
Read the release notes and close Unreal
before replacing the plugin folder.

18
00:01:24.253 --> 00:01:27.176
For help and release notes,
return to the beta page.

19
00:01:27.526 --> 00:01:32.902
Donations to Alex's Lab are optional.
You can repeat the guided tutorial at any time.
